\description{
Manage report modules in camtrapReport. These functions can be used to list
existing modules, add new modules, move modules within the report structure,
remove modules, restore deleted modules, and empty the module trash.
}
\details{
camtrapReport uses a modular report architecture in which each report section
is stored as a module. A module can contain section metadata, text,
executable R code, required packages, and rendering settings.

\code{add_Module()} adds a new YAML-defined module to an explicitly
supplied writable module directory. The module can optionally be
inserted before or after an existing module.

\code{move_Module()} changes the position or parent of an existing module within
the hierarchical report structure.

\code{remove_Module()} moves a module to the module trash. If \code{recursive = TRUE},
child modules are also moved to the trash.

\code{restore_Module()} restores a previously removed module from the trash.

\code{empty_trash()} permanently removes modules from the trash.

\code{list_Modules()} lists active modules and can optionally include deleted
modules stored in the trash.
}
